    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see what you did there with the repetition. The indexer score went up slightly, but honestly, it's getting a bit repetitive to read the same dates over and over in every sentence. \n\nLet's try one more batch to see if we can get it right. This next set of files is much longer and has a lot more dates. I really need a summary that is actually readable and professional for the researchers, but I also can't have the indexer score being too low or the metadata will be useless. \n\nCan you give me a summary for this text? Please try to weave the dates in naturally so it doesn't feel like you're just stuffing them in, but definitely ensure the indexer sees plenty of them.\n\n\"The records show a period of intense negotiation. On the 12th of January, 1843, the first memorandum was signed. This was followed by a series of heated exchanges on the 15th of February, 1843, and the 28th of March, 1843. By the time the spring thaw arrived on 10/04/1843, the situation had stabilized slightly. However, a sudden tariff hike on 22/05/1843 caused renewed protests, which lasted until the final treaty was ratified on 15/08/1843.\"",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
